As stated in another thread on ascension statistics, knights are boring. 
Currently, I have a knight ready to make the run. I have the following 
observations and suggestions:
1) The Quest is a farce --
    a) first King Arthur greets you telling you about the remains of a 
large battle you saw on the way into his castle. Should not the field on 
the first level of the knights quest then be littered with 
damaged/undamaged armor and weapons and a few scared horses?
    b) Should not the field on the first level have a cemetery or 
scattered graves of fallen knights in this huge battle?
    c) A guaranteed lance would be appropriate since those damn things 
shatter like a cheap beer glass.
    d) should not the first level of the quest also have a room full of 
lances and a couple of saddles?
    e) For a dragon, Ixoth's stash is anemic

2) Non-dragon mounts should be capable of having dragon scale armor. 
Apply the scales to the mount, apply the saddle, sit on the mount 
wearing no armor, and read a ?oEnchant Armor. (A black dragon just 
disintegrated my Blue Dragon mount AND the saddle -- I am quite annoyed)
3) Merlin's mirror should have an Invoking aspect which charms d3 
monsters which can be ridden. I have been trying to play the knight 
riding a mount as often as possible; but, the inability to tame other 
than horses is a daunting task.
4) Would it be illogical for a wood golem to generate a lance occasionally?

Comments?


